function regexPanel(){const m=model();toolbar([['Expression → NFA',()=>{m.expression=$('#expression')?.value??m.expression;add(A.regexToFA(m.expression));},'primary']]);$('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel split"><div><label class="field"><span>Regular expression</span><textarea id="expression" rows="5" spellcheck="false">${E(m.expression)}</textarea></label><p class="hint">+ union · juxtaposition concatenation · * repetition · ( ) grouping · λ empty string · ∅ empty language. This is formal-language notation, not JavaScript regex syntax.</p><label class="field"><span>Test inputs · one per line</span><textarea id="regex-inputs" rows="5">ab\naab\nba\nλ</textarea></label><div id="regex-actions"></div></div><div id="regex-results"><div class="card"><h3>From an expression to a machine</h3><p>Thompson construction creates small fragments for symbols, then connects them with empty transitions for concatenation, union and repetition. Convert the result to a DFA or minimize it from the Convert menu.</p></div></div></div>`;$('#expression').onchange=()=>{checkpoint();m.expression=$('#expression').value;changed();};$('#regex-actions').append(button('Test expression',()=>{m.expression=$('#expression').value;changed();const fa=A.regexToFA(m.expression);$('#regex-results').innerHTML='<table><tr><th>Input</th><th>Result</th></tr>'+$('#regex-inputs').value.split('\n').map(s=>`<tr><td>${E(s||'λ')}</td><td>${simulate(fa,A.empty(s)).status}</td></tr>`).join('')+'</table>';},'primary'));}
function lsystemPanel(){const m=model();toolbar([['Render system',()=>{if($('#ls-axiom'))applyLSystem();tab='Render';render();},'primary']]);if(tab==='Editor'){$('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel split"><div><label class="field"><span>Axiom · space-delimited symbols</span><input id="ls-axiom" value="${E(m.axiom)}"></label><label class="field"><span>Rewriting rules · one per line</span><textarea id="ls-rules" rows="8">${E(m.productions.map(p=>p.left+' → '+p.right).join('\n'))}</textarea></label><button id="ls-apply">Apply changes</button></div><div><label class="field"><span>Drawing parameters · name = value</span><textarea id="ls-params" rows="9">${E(Object.entries(m.parameters).map(([k,v])=>k+' = '+v).join('\n'))}</textarea></label><p class="hint">g draws; f moves; + − turn; &amp; ^ pitch; / * roll; [ ] branch; { } polygon; ! ~ width. Commands can take numeric expressions such as g(distance*2). Context rule example: 1 a X b → g.</p></div></div>`;$('#ls-apply').onclick=safe(()=>{applyLSystem();changed('L-system applied.');});return;}
 $('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="row"><label>Depth <input id="ls-depth" type="number" min="0" max="10" value="4" style="width:65px"></label><label>View X <input id="view-x" type="range" min="-180" max="180" value="0"></label><label>View Y <input id="view-y" type="range" min="-180" max="180" value="0"></label><button id="ls-draw" class="primary">Draw</button><button id="ls-export">Export SVG</button><span id="ls-count" class="hint"></span></div><svg id="ls-svg" class="diagram-small" style="height:430px" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg><details><summary>Expanded symbols</summary><pre id="ls-word" class="scroll"></pre></details></div>`;
 const paint=()=>{const depth=Math.max(0,Math.min(10,+$('#ls-depth').value)),word=expand(m.axiom,m.productions,depth),shapes=turtle(word,m.parameters,[+$('#view-x').value,+$('#view-y').value,0]),all=shapes.flatMap(s=>s.points),xs=all.map(p=>p[0]),ys=all.map(p=>p[1]),minX=xs.length?Math.min(...xs):-10,maxX=xs.length?Math.max(...xs):10,minY=ys.length?Math.min(...ys):-10,maxY=ys.length?Math.max(...ys):10;$('#ls-svg').setAttribute('viewBox',`${minX-20} ${-maxY-20} ${Math.max(40,maxX-minX+40)} ${Math.max(40,maxY-minY+40)}`);$('#ls-svg').innerHTML=shapes.map(s=>`<${s.polygon?'polygon':'polyline'} points="${s.points.map(p=>p[0]+','+-p[1]).join(' ')}" fill="${s.polygon?E(s.color):'none'}" stroke="${s.polygon?'none':E(s.color)}" stroke-width="${s.width||1}" stroke-linecap="round"/>`).join('');$('#ls-count').textContent=word.length+' symbols · '+shapes.length+' shapes';$('#ls-word').textContent=word.slice(0,10000).join(' ')+(word.length>10000?' … display truncated':'');};$('#ls-draw').onclick=safe(paint);$('#ls-export').onclick=()=>download($('#ls-svg').outerHTML,'lsystem.svg','image/svg+xml');safe(paint)();}
function applyLSystem(){const productions=$('#ls-rules').value.split('\n').filter(s=>s.trim()).map(line=>{const parts=line.split(/→|->/);if(parts.length!==2)throw Error('Use left → right for L-system rules.');return{left:parts[0].trim(),right:A.empty(parts[1].trim())};}),parameters=Object.fromEntries($('#ls-params').value.split('\n').filter(s=>s.trim()).map(line=>{const i=line.indexOf('=');if(i<1)throw Error('Use name = value for parameters.');return[line.slice(0,i).trim(),line.slice(i+1).trim()];}));checkpoint();Object.assign(model(),{axiom:$('#ls-axiom').value,productions,parameters});persist();}
function pumpingPanel(){const cf=model().type==='pumpingcf',list=languages.filter(l=>l.cf===cf),names=cf?['u','v','x','y','z']:['x','y','z'];toolbar([],cf?'Context-free lemma: w = uvxyz, |vxy| ≤ m, |vy| > 0':'Regular lemma: w = xyz, |xy| ≤ m, |y| > 0');$('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel split"><div><label class="field"><span>Language</span><select id="pump-language">${list.map(l=>`<option value="${l.id}" ${model().language===l.id?'selected':''}>${E(l.label)}</option>`).join('')}</select></label><div class="row"><label class="field"><span>Pumping length m</span><input id="pump-m" type="number" min="1" max="20" value="3"></label><button id="pump-witness">Computer chooses a word</button></div><label class="field"><span>Witness word w</span><input id="pump-word" value="${cf?'aaabbbccc':'aaaaaa'}"></label><div class="row">${names.map(n=>`<label class="field" style="flex:1;min-width:60px"><span>${n}</span><input id="part-${n}" style="width:100%" value=""></label>`).join('')}</div><div class="row"><label class="field"><span>Exponent i</span><input id="pump-i" type="number" min="0" max="100" value="0"></label></div><div id="pump-actions" class="actions"></div></div><div><div id="pump-result"></div><div class="card"><h3>What does this demonstrate?</h3><p>To challenge regularity (or context-freeness), choose a witness in the language. The other player chooses a valid decomposition. Then find an exponent that moves the word outside the language.</p><p>A failed decomposition is a counterexample to that decomposition. Checking a few exponents cannot prove a language regular or context-free. The computer’s split search tests i = 0, 2, 3, 4 and is explicitly a bounded aid.</p></div></div></div>`;const lang=()=>list.find(l=>l.id===$('#pump-language').value),sample=()=>{$('#pump-word').value=lang().sample(Math.max(1,Math.min(20,+$('#pump-m').value)));names.forEach(n=>$('#part-'+n).value='');model().language=lang().id;persist();};$('#pump-witness').onclick=safe(sample);$('#pump-language').onchange=sample;sample();$('#pump-actions').append(button('Pump word',()=>{const r=pump(lang(),$('#pump-word').value,names.map(n=>$('#part-'+n).value),+$('#pump-m').value,+$('#pump-i').value,cf);$('#pump-result').innerHTML=`<div class="result ${r.belongs?'accepted':'rejected'}">${r.belongs?'Still in the language':'Outside the language'}</div><pre>${E(r.word||'λ')}</pre>`;},'primary'),button('Computer chooses a split',()=>{const parts=findSplit(lang(),$('#pump-word').value,+$('#pump-m').value,cf);if(parts){names.forEach((n,i)=>$('#part-'+n).value=parts[i]);$('#pump-result').innerHTML='<div class="result">Candidate survives i = 0, 2, 3, 4. This is not a proof for all exponents.</div>';}else $('#pump-result').innerHTML='<div class="result rejected">No split survives the tested exponents within the search bounds.</div>';}));}
async function exportImage(format){if(!isMachine())throw Error('Image export is available for automata; L-systems have their own SVG export.');const css=[...document.styleSheets].flatMap(s=>{try{return[...s.cssRules].map(r=>r.cssText);}catch{return[];}}).join('\n');const svg=`<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1000 650" width="1000" height="650"><style>${css}</style><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="white"/>${graphMarkup()}</svg>`;if(format==='svg')download(svg,model().name+'.svg','image/svg+xml');else{const img=new Image(),url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([svg],{type:'image/svg+xml'}));img.onload=()=>{const canvas=document.createElement('canvas');canvas.width=1000;canvas.height=650;canvas.getContext('2d').drawImage(img,0,0);URL.revokeObjectURL(url);canvas.toBlob(blob=>{const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(blob);a.download=model().name+'.png';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000);});};img.src=url;}}
function guide(){message('Welcome to the formal languages lab',`<p class="hint">A browser reconstruction informed by JFLAP 7.1’s shipped help and bytecode. Documents stay in this browser until you save or export them.</p><div class="help-grid"><section><h3>01 · Draw a machine</h3><p>Select State, then click to place states. Select Transition and drag between states, including a state to itself. Right-click or double-click a state to set initial/final flags. Double-click transitions to edit their fields. Select an edge to drag its curve handle.</p></section><section><h3>02 · Run and inspect</h3><p>Use Simulate for individual steps and fast runs, Multiple Run for batches, and Inspect for highlights. A configuration includes the current state, input position and any stack, tape or output. Search limits remain inconclusive.</p></section><section><h3>03 · Convert structures</h3><p>The Convert menu includes subset construction, minimization, FA/grammar/expression conversions and top-down or bottom-up CFG-to-PDA conversion. Results open as new documents.</p></section><section><h3>04 · Explore a grammar</h3><p>Uppercase letters are variables. Write one production per line; λ is the empty word. The first rule sets the start variable. FIRST/FOLLOW, LL(1), SLR, brute derivations and CYK are available from Parse.</p></section><section><h3>05 · Render an L-system</h3><p>Separate symbols with spaces. g draws, f moves, +/− turn, brackets save and restore turtle state. Render controls include rewriting depth and 3D viewing rotations.</p></section><section><h3>06 · Test pumping arguments</h3><p>Choose a language and pumping length. Supply or generate a witness, split it, and test exponents. The workbench distinguishes finite experiments from universal proofs.</p></section></div><p class="hint"><a href="docs/GUIDE.html" target="_blank">Detailed feature and evidence guide</a> · <a href="docs/COVERAGE.md" target="_blank">Compatibility and known differences</a> · <a href="tests/index.html" target="_blank">Run algorithm regression tests</a></p>`);}
$('#new').onclick=newStructure;$('#help').onclick=guide;$('#open').onclick=()=>$('#file').click();$('#save').onclick=safe(()=>save());$('#example').onclick=safe(()=>add(example(model().type==='turing'&&model().tapes>1?'multitape':model().type)));$('#file').onchange=safe(async e=>{for(const file of e.target.files){if(file.size>5*1024*1024)throw Error('Choose a model smaller than 5 MB.');add(deserialize(await file.text(),file.name.replace(/\.[^.]+$/,'')));}e.target.value='';});
document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if($('#dialog').open||['INPUT','TEXTAREA','SELECT'].includes(e.target.tagName))return;if((e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey)&&e.key.toLowerCase()==='s'){e.preventDefault();safe(()=>save())();}else if((e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey)&&e.key.toLowerCase()==='z'){e.preventDefault();e.shiftKey?doRedo():doUndo();}else if(isMachine()&&tab==='Editor'){const tools={a:'select',s:'state',t:'transition',d:'delete'};if(tools[e.key.toLowerCase()]){tool=tools[e.key.toLowerCase()];editor();}}});
render();

function simulationGraph(r){
 const host=$('#simulation-graph');if(!host)return;
 const configs=r.accepted.length?r.accepted:r.frontier,paths=new Map([['[]',[]]]);
 configs.forEach(c=>(c.path||[]).forEach((_,i)=>{const path=c.path.slice(0,i+1);paths.set(JSON.stringify(path),path);}));
 const previous=$('#simulation-level')?.value;
 host.innerHTML='<label class="field"><span>Machine view</span><select id="simulation-level">'+[...paths].map(([key,path])=>`<option value="${E(key)}">${path.length?'Block '+E(path.join(' / ')):'Root machine'}</option>`).join('')+'</select></label><svg class="diagram-small" id="simulation-canvas" role="img" aria-label="Live simulation graph"></svg><p class="hint">Highlighted states contain current configurations. Choose a block to inspect nested execution.</p>';
 const chooser=$('#simulation-level');if(paths.has(previous))chooser.value=previous;
 const paint=()=>{const path=paths.get(chooser.value),m=path.reduce((m,id)=>m.states.find(s=>s.id===id).block,r.m),marks=configs.filter(c=>path.every((id,i)=>c.path?.[i]===id)).map(c=>c.path?.length>path.length?c.path[path.length]:c.state),svg=$('#simulation-canvas');
 const xs=m.states.map(s=>s.x),ys=m.states.map(s=>s.y),left=Math.min(0,...xs)-90,top=Math.min(0,...ys)-130;
 svg.setAttribute('viewBox',`${left} ${top} ${Math.max(200,...xs)-left+90} ${Math.max(180,...ys)-top+90}`);svg.innerHTML=graphMarkup(m,marks,null);
 };chooser.onchange=paint;paint();
}

function batchPanel(){
 toolbar([], 'Run the same input strings against several machines of one type.');
 const machines=docs.map((m,i)=>({m,i})).filter(({m})=>Array.isArray(m.states)&&!batchSession.excluded.has(m));batchSession.selected??=new Set(machines.filter(({m})=>m.type===model().type).map(({m})=>m));let results=null,selectedModels=[];
 $('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="split"><section><h3>Machines to compare</h3><label class="field"><span>Add machine files</span><input type="file" id="batch-add-files" accept=".jff,.xml,.json" multiple></label><button id="batch-restore">Show all open machines</button><div id="batch-machines">${machines.map(({m,i})=>`<label class="field"><span><input type="checkbox" data-batch-machine="${i}" ${batchSession.selected.has(m)?'checked':''}> ${E(m.name)} · ${E(types[m.type])}</span></label><div class="actions"><button data-batch-edit="${i}">Edit ${E(m.name)}</button><button data-batch-remove="${i}">Remove ${E(m.name)} from batch</button></div>`).join('')||'<p>Open or create a machine first.</p>'}</div><label class="field"><span>PDA acceptance</span><select id="batch-pda-mode"><option value="final">Final state</option><option value="empty">Empty stack</option></select></label></section><section><label class="field"><span>Shared inputs · one per line</span><textarea id="shared-inputs" rows="7">${E(batchSession.inputs??model().batch??'λ\n0\n1\n01')}</textarea></label><label class="field"><span>Load shared input file</span><input type="file" id="batch-input-file" accept=".txt,.in,text/plain"></label><div id="batch-actions" class="actions"></div></section></div><div id="batch-matrix" class="scroll"></div></div>`;
 $('#shared-inputs').oninput=()=>{batchSession.inputs=$('#shared-inputs').value;};
 $('#batch-machines').querySelectorAll('[data-batch-machine]').forEach(el=>el.onchange=()=>{const m=docs[+el.dataset.batchMachine];el.checked?batchSession.selected.add(m):batchSession.selected.delete(m);});
 $('#batch-machines').querySelectorAll('[data-batch-edit]').forEach(el=>el.onclick=()=>{active=+el.dataset.batchEdit;blockParents=[];runner=null;undo=[];redo=[];tab='Editor';render();});
 $('#batch-machines').querySelectorAll('[data-batch-remove]').forEach(el=>el.onclick=()=>{const m=docs[+el.dataset.batchRemove];batchSession.excluded.add(m);batchSession.selected.delete(m);batchPanel();});
 $('#batch-restore').onclick=()=>{batchSession.excluded.clear();batchPanel();};
 $('#batch-add-files').onchange=safe(async e=>{const imported=[];for(const file of e.target.files){if(file.size>5*1024*1024)throw Error('Choose models smaller than 5 MB.');const m=deserialize(await file.text(),file.name.replace(/\.[^.]+$/,''));if(!Array.isArray(m.states))throw Error(file.name+' is not a machine.');imported.push(m);}for(const m of imported){docs.push(m);batchSession.selected.add(m);}persist();render();status(imported.length+' machines added to batch.');});
 $('#batch-input-file').onchange=safe(async e=>{const file=e.target.files[0];if(!file)return;if(file.size>5*1024*1024)throw Error('Choose inputs smaller than 5 MB.');batchSession.inputs=parseInputs(await file.text()).join('\n');$('#shared-inputs').value=batchSession.inputs;status('Shared inputs loaded.');e.target.value='';});
 $('#batch-actions').append(button('Run batch',()=>{selectedModels=[...$('#batch-machines').querySelectorAll('[data-batch-machine]:checked')].map(el=>docs[+el.dataset.batchMachine]);results=runBatch(selectedModels,parseInputs($('#shared-inputs').value),{...prefs,acceptance:selectedModels[0]?.type==='pda'?$('#batch-pda-mode').value:prefs.acceptance});model().batch=$('#shared-inputs').value;persist();$('#batch-matrix').innerHTML='<table><caption>'+results.length+' inputs × '+selectedModels.length+' machines</caption><thead><tr><th>Input</th>'+selectedModels.map(m=>'<th>'+E(m.name)+'</th>').join('')+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+results.map(row=>'<tr><th>'+E(row.input||'λ')+'</th>'+row.results.map(r=>'<td>'+E(r.status)+(r.error?'<br>'+E(r.error):r.outputs?.length?'<br><small>'+E(JSON.stringify(r.outputs))+'</small>':'')+'</td>').join('')+'</tr>').join('')+'</tbody></table>';},'primary'),button('Export batch CSV',()=>{if(!results)throw Error('Run the batch first.');download(batchCSV(selectedModels,results),'batch-results.csv','text/csv');}));
}

function grammarBatchPanel(){
 const m=model();let rows=[];toolbar([], 'Brute-force derivations for multiple inputs. Search limits remain inconclusive.');
 $('#content').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="split"><section><label class="field"><span>Grammar inputs · one per line</span><textarea id="grammar-batch-inputs" rows="7">${E(m.parseBatch??'λ\nab\naabb\naab')}</textarea></label><label class="field"><span>Load grammar inputs</span><input id="grammar-input-file" type="file" accept=".txt,.in,text/plain"></label><div id="grammar-batch-actions" class="actions"></div></section><section id="grammar-batch-results" class="scroll"></section></div><h3>Selected derivation</h3><div id="parse-output" class="scroll"></div></div>`;
 $('#grammar-input-file').onchange=safe(async e=>{const file=e.target.files[0];if(!file)return;if(file.size>5*1024*1024)throw Error('Choose inputs smaller than 5 MB.');$('#grammar-batch-inputs').value=parseInputs(await file.text()).join('\n');e.target.value='';});
 $('#grammar-batch-actions').append(button('Parse all inputs',()=>{m.parseBatch=$('#grammar-batch-inputs').value;persist();rows=parseGrammarBatch(m.productions,parseInputs(m.parseBatch),prefs.limit);$('#parse-output').replaceChildren();$('#grammar-batch-results').innerHTML='<table><caption>'+rows.length+' inputs</caption><tr><th>Input</th><th>Result</th><th>Details</th></tr>'+rows.map((r,i)=>`<tr><td>${E(r.input||'λ')}</td><td>${E(r.status)}${r.error?'<br>'+E(r.error):''}</td><td><button data-derivation="${i}">View derivation ${i+1}</button></td></tr>`).join('')+'</table>';$('#grammar-batch-results').querySelectorAll('[data-derivation]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>showDerivation(rows[+b.dataset.derivation].rows||[]));},'primary'));
}
